What was done: the 67,652 nonstop routes (11 with stops left out) matched
to their airports by IATA code (729 routes whose code the airport database
no longer holds, and one route from an airport to itself, left out); both
directions of a route kept as one pair of airports; the airlines flying the
pair counted, a codeshare (sold by one airline, flown by another) not
counted as a second airline, and a pair sold only as a codeshare counted as
one airline; the great-circle distance added, sorted into short haul (under
1,500 km), medium haul and long haul (4,000 km or more); domestic when both
airports are in the same country; each pair oriented from the airport with
more nonstop destinations; positions rounded to four decimal places. Only
the airport code, city, country and name are kept from the airport
database. The airline database is not used.


